Register the bootstrap Rust toolchains under `@rules_rust//rust:bootstrap_toolchain_type`.

Companion patch: rules_rust-bootstrap-toolchain-type.patch. Apply both, or neither. That patch explains the problem in
full. This is a summary.

# The problem

rules_rust builds `@rules_rust//util/process_wrapper:process_wrapper` with the `_bootstrap` Rust toolchain. Before,
the build setting `@rules_rust//rust/private:bootstrap_setting` selected that toolchain. `declare_rustc_toolchains` put
the config setting `:bootstrapping` or `:bootstrapped` in the `target_settings` of each toolchain.

The process wrapper set the setting with a rule transition. That transition also changed the configuration of the cc
toolchain and of its runtime libraries. So Bazel built compiler-rt two times for each exec platform:

    bazel-out/darwin_arm64-opt-exec-ST-2ca6e5d5978b/.../compiler-rt   281 actions   <- normal exec
    bazel-out/darwin_arm64-opt-exec-ST-2555a4bcebed/.../compiler-rt   281 actions   <- exec + bootstrap_setting=true

# The fix

The rules_rust patch removes the transition and adds the toolchain type `@rules_rust//rust:bootstrap_toolchain_type`.
This patch registers the toolchains to match:

    toolchain(
        name = "default_macos_aarch64_to_non_bpf_targets_1_93_1",
        toolchain = "default_macos_aarch64_1_93_1_rust_toolchain",
        toolchain_type = "@rules_rust//rust:toolchain_type",
        target_settings = [<target triples>, "@rules_rs//rs/toolchains:non_bpf_targets", <channel>],
    )

    toolchain(
        name = "default_macos_aarch64_to_non_bpf_targets_1_93_1_bootstrap",
        toolchain = "default_macos_aarch64_1_93_1_rust_toolchain_bootstrap",
        toolchain_type = "@rules_rust//rust:bootstrap_toolchain_type",
        target_settings = [<target triples>, "@rules_rs//rs/toolchains:non_bpf_targets", <channel>],
    )

The `:bootstrapping` and `:bootstrapped` entries are gone from `target_settings`. The toolchain type alone now
separates the two toolchains. The BPF toolchain has no bootstrap variant, and it stays on
`@rules_rust//rust:toolchain_type`.

The selection tests now resolve the bootstrap cases through `_resolved_bootstrap_toolchain`, a rule that asks for
the bootstrap type. They do not set `bootstrap_setting` now.

# What does not change

- `rs/private/source_stdlib.bzl` still writes `bootstrap_setting = False`. rules_rust keeps the setting as a no-op, so
  this transition still loads, and it has no effect.
- The `@rules_rs//rs/toolchains:all_targets` alias still selects on `:bootstrapped`. The setting is always false now,
  so the alias always takes the `:bootstrapped` branch, as before for all targets except the process wrapper.

diff --git a/rs/toolchains/declare_rustc_toolchains.bzl b/rs/toolchains/declare_rustc_toolchains.bzl
--- a/rs/toolchains/declare_rustc_toolchains.bzl
+++ b/rs/toolchains/declare_rustc_toolchains.bzl
@@ -290,7 +290,6 @@ def declare_rustc_toolchains(
         ]:
             target_kind = "bpf" if is_bpf else "non_bpf"
             bootstrap_suffix = "_bootstrap" if bootstrapping else ""
-            bootstrap_setting = "@rules_rust//rust/private:" + ("bootstrapping" if bootstrapping else "bootstrapped")
             toolchain_suffix = "_bpf" if is_bpf else bootstrap_suffix
             native.toolchain(
                 name = name + "_{}_{}_to_{}_targets_{}{}".format(
@@ -303,9 +302,11 @@ def declare_rustc_toolchains(
                 exec_compatible_with = exec_compatible_with,
                 target_settings = target_settings + [
                     "@rules_rs//rs/toolchains:bpf_targets" if is_bpf else "@rules_rs//rs/toolchains:non_bpf_targets",
-                    bootstrap_setting,
                 ],
                 toolchain = rust_toolchain_name + toolchain_suffix,
-                toolchain_type = "@rules_rust//rust:toolchain_type",
+                # The `*_without_process_wrapper` rules of rules_rust ask for the bootstrap toolchain type. A build
+                # setting does not select the bootstrap toolchain, so the process wrapper keeps the configuration of
+                # the targets that use it.
+                toolchain_type = "@rules_rust//rust:bootstrap_toolchain_type" if bootstrapping else "@rules_rust//rust:toolchain_type",
                 visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
             )
diff --git a/rs/toolchains/tests/declare_rustc_toolchains_test.bzl b/rs/toolchains/tests/declare_rustc_toolchains_test.bzl
--- a/rs/toolchains/tests/declare_rustc_toolchains_test.bzl
+++ b/rs/toolchains/tests/declare_rustc_toolchains_test.bzl
@@ -4,9 +4,9 @@ load("@bazel_skylib//lib:unittest.bzl", "analysistest", "asserts")
 load("//rs/toolchains:declare_rustc_toolchains.bzl", "declare_rustc_toolchains")
 
 _RUST_TOOLCHAIN = "@rules_rust//rust:toolchain_type"
+_RUST_BOOTSTRAP_TOOLCHAIN = "@rules_rust//rust:bootstrap_toolchain_type"
 _CARGO_TOOLCHAIN = "@rules_rust//cargo:toolchain_type"
 _PLATFORM = "//command_line_option:platforms"
-_BOOTSTRAP = str(Label("@rules_rust//rust/private:bootstrap_setting"))
 _SOURCE_STDLIB = str(Label("//rs/private:source_stdlib_building"))
 _PACKAGE = "//rs/toolchains/tests:"
 
@@ -23,6 +23,17 @@ _resolved_toolchain = rule(
     toolchains = [_RUST_TOOLCHAIN, _CARGO_TOOLCHAIN],
 )
 
+def _resolved_bootstrap_toolchain_impl(ctx):
+    return [_ResolvedToolchains(
+        rust = ctx.toolchains[_RUST_BOOTSTRAP_TOOLCHAIN],
+        cargo = ctx.toolchains[_CARGO_TOOLCHAIN],
+    )]
+
+_resolved_bootstrap_toolchain = rule(
+    implementation = _resolved_bootstrap_toolchain_impl,
+    toolchains = [_RUST_BOOTSTRAP_TOOLCHAIN, _CARGO_TOOLCHAIN],
+)
+
 def _selection_test_impl(ctx):
     env = analysistest.begin(ctx)
     resolved = analysistest.target_under_test(env)[_ResolvedToolchains]
@@ -59,7 +70,6 @@ def _selection_test(triple, bootstrap = False, exec_triple = "x86_64-unknown-lin
         },
         config_settings = {
             _PLATFORM: str(Label("//rs/platforms:" + triple)),
-            _BOOTSTRAP: bootstrap,
             # Analyze BPF toolchain selection without building its source stdlib.
             _SOURCE_STDLIB: True,
             "//command_line_option:extra_execution_platforms": [str(Label("//rs/platforms:" + exec_triple))],
@@ -140,6 +150,7 @@ def declare_rustc_toolchains_test_suite(name):
         tags = ["manual"],
     )
     _resolved_toolchain(name = "resolved_toolchain", tags = ["manual"])
+    _resolved_bootstrap_toolchain(name = "resolved_bootstrap_toolchain", tags = ["manual"])
 
     tests = []
     for test_name, test_rule, kwargs in [
@@ -160,7 +171,7 @@ def declare_rustc_toolchains_test_suite(name):
     ]:
         test_rule(
             name = test_name + "_test",
-            target_under_test = ":resolved_toolchain",
+            target_under_test = ":resolved_bootstrap_toolchain" if "bootstrap" in test_name else ":resolved_toolchain",
             **kwargs
         )
         tests.append(":" + test_name + "_test")
